{"i":0,"start_s":0.18,"end_s":1,"speaker":"SPEAKER_02","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":true,"text":"Gentlemen,"}
{"i":1,"start_s":1,"end_s":4.33,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"recognize for one minute. Thank you, Madam"}
{"i":2,"start_s":4.33,"end_s":5.24,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"Speaker. It"}
{"i":3,"start_s":5.32,"end_s":28.26,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"was with great sadness that West Michigan learned on Friday of the passing of our first lady, Betty Ford. The first lady spent most of her life in Grand Rapids. A graduate of Central High School, she worked in a department store downtown and was a dance instructor. Early on, Mrs. Ford showed her heart for the disadvantage in our community, teaching dance to children who are physically disabled, deaf, and blind."}
{"i":4,"start_s":28.41,"end_s":28.47,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"A"}
{"i":5,"start_s":28.9,"end_s":39.9,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"mutual friend introduced Mrs. Ford to Jerry in 1947. A successful lawyer and former star of the University of Michigan's football team, the future president was not quite in public life when they met."}
{"i":6,"start_s":39.94,"end_s":40.21,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"No one"}
{"i":7,"start_s":40.4,"end_s":47.11,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"could have foreseen the set of circumstances that thrust the Fords into the White House. But Mrs. Ford took the challenge with"}
{"i":8,"start_s":47.11,"end_s":47.82,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"gusto. And as"}
{"i":9,"start_s":48,"end_s":53.94,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"First Lady, she revealed many of her struggles to the public so that she could help others with similar difficulties."}
{"i":10,"start_s":53.92,"end_s":59.3,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"low","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"In the 1970s, she publicly spoke about her battle with breast cancer, which was not often discussed during that time."}
{"i":11,"start_s":59.58,"end_s":60.05,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"And in the"}
{"i":12,"start_s":60.05,"end_s":77.4,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"1980s, she took the lessons she learned battling alcoholism to found a number of foundations and institutes dedicated to helping others with the condition. Betty Ford honored West Michigan with her public service, humor, and grace. We are proud to have called such a fine citizen one of our own. I yield back."}
{"i":13,"start_s":77.75,"end_s":78.82,"speaker":null,"speaker_conf":"none","speaker_cause":"no_turn_overlap","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"The gentleman"}
{"i":14,"start_s":78.82,"end_s":80.25,"speaker":"SPEAKER_01","speaker_conf":"high","overlap":false,"low_conf":false,"text":"yields back."}
